       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error.\n\n**The problem:** Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is 5 times the usual maximum adult dose of 200 mg/day. The usual adult range is 50\u2013200 mg/day, often starting at 25\u201350 mg. A daily dose of 1000 mg would be in overdose territory, with risk of serotonin syndrome, QTc prolongation and seizures. This looks like it could be an extra zero, and you may have meant **100 mg**.\n\n**Could you confirm which you meant?**\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg PO once daily.** I'll enter this as soon as you confirm.\n2. **A different dose.** Tell me the amount and I'll enter it.\n3. **1000 mg was intended.** I'd still strongly recommend talking with pharmacy before this goes in, since it's far above any standard dosing."
